{"id":"resp_8ff7de92379fbe43","created_at":1795542992,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_9d879a5b2dc5e800","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to repair the previous candidate SHACL based on findings. Findings:\n\n1. ADMISSION_SCOPE_ERROR: Other target classes select beyond declared population. The issue: sh:targetClass nltl:ship? Actually targetClass for ShipBoundaryShape is nltl:ship, which is correct (owner_class defined as https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship). However also we have sh:targetClass for HullBoundaryPointShape set to nltl:hullBoundaryPoint, which may be outside the declared population (focus_set only includes ship class). The admission mechanism likely expects only ship class as target; other target classes need activation condition to restrict to population? Usually we should use sh:targetSubjectsOf to restrict based on property from ship. Instead of declaring a targetClass for hullBoundaryPoint, we can embed the property shape directly in ShipBoundaryShape with path to hullBoundaryPoint and then nested shapes. To avoid selecting hullBoundaryPoint instances globally. So we need to remove sh:targetClass on hullBoundaryPoint shapes, maybe make them node shapes without targetClass, and reference via sh:node.\n\nSimilarly ShellInclinationQuantityShape has targetClass qudt:QuantityValue, also outside declared population. Should be node shape without targetClass.\n\nThus fix ADMISSION_SCOPE_ERROR by removing sh:targetClass from those shapes.\n\n2. UNRESOLVED_CONTEXT: Target cannot be bound to explicit model owner. For sh:targetClass line 42 column 20 (likely the HullBoundaryPointShape). So similar fix.\n\n3. NUMERIC_TERM_REVIEW: Need decide whether exact RDF term required or numeric equality. Since source says \"angle is 7° from horizontal\" - likely numeric equality needed. In SHACL, sh:hasValue does exact term, which is fine. But maybe need to use sh:equals? The suggestion: If source requires numeric equality, use numeric comparison while retaining datatype and units. Use sh:equal to? Actually SHACL has sh:equals? For numeric comparison, we can use sh:in or sh:minInclusive/sh:maxInclusive. For exact value, we could use sh:hasValue with xsd:decimal \"7\". That's fine. However need to ensure datatype decimal, and unit must be DEG. Maybe also need to accept numeric equivalence like \"7.0\". sh:hasValue with \"7\"^^decimal matches only that literal. To be safe, we can enforce sh:equals with sh:datatype and also use sh:minInclusive and sh:maxInclusive of 7, to allow equivalents. But guideline says preserve required datatype and units. Could add sh:equals for numeric equality using sh:hasValue is okay.\n\nThus maybe adjust to use sh:hasValue with datatype decimal, fine.\n\nPotential other issues: missing sh:node for quantity shape: they used sh:node _:ShellInclinationQuantityShape within HullBoundaryPointShape property, fine.\n\nBut with removal of targetClass, we need to ensure shapes are still reachable via node constraint.\n\nThus final revised SHACL:\n\n- Define ShipBoundaryShape with targetClass nltl:ship and has property linking to hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint with sh:node _:HullBoundaryPointShape.\n\n- Define HullBoundaryPointShape as a node shape (no targetClass) with property shellInclinationAngle sh:node _:ShellInclinationQuantityShape.\n\n- Define ShellInclinationQuantityShape as node shape (no targetClass) with two property constraints: numericValue must be 7 decimal, and unit must be unit:DEG.\n\nAlso adjust prefixes: nltl: => https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab# ; ensure consistent.\n\nPotential additional: The property path for unit: use qudt:unit, needs to have sh:hasValue unit:DEG. Ensure unit prefix defined.\n\nAlso incorporate messages.\n\nNow produce final block <BEGIN_SHACL> ... <END_SHACL>. Ensure no extra characters.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_9d71bbcc32174b47","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for a ship that must have a bottom‑region / lower‑region\n# boundary point whose shell inclination angle is exactly 7 deg.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:ShipBoundaryShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node _:HullBoundaryPointShape ;\n        sh:message \"A ship must have at least one bottom‑region / lower‑region boundary point.\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for the hull boundary point linked from the ship.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:HullBoundaryPointShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:shellInclinationAngle ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node _:ShellInclinationQuantityShape ;\n        sh:message \"The hull boundary point must have a shell inclination angle.\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for the QuantityValue that encodes the shell inclination angle.\n# The value must be 7 deg.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:ShellInclinationQuantityShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:hasValue \"7\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:message \"Shell inclination angle numeric value must be 7 (decimal).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:hasValue unit:DEG ;\n        sh:message \"Shell inclination angle unit must be degree (DEG).\" ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":22228,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":64,"cache_write_tokens":22160,"input_tokens_per_turn":[22228],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[64]},"output_tokens":1317,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":802,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1317],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":23545},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}